\textbf{Case 2.} There exists $c>0$ such that $\tilde{\lambda}(s)\geq c$.
In this case, Theorem \ref{t9.16} implies that $\lambda(s)>\tilde{c}$ for some constant $\tilde{c}>0$.
By rescaling, we can set
\begin{align}\label{qdz}
1\leq \lambda(s)\leq \frac{1}{\tilde{c}},\quad \forall\,  s>0.
